  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The agent found all three abort points: grep's no-match exit carried through pipefail, cmp's exit 1 on a difference, and the slugify.sh capture failing. It guarded each one at the command that is expected to exit non-zero (if-capture or `|| true`), so each failure is recorded as one FAIL, the run continues and still exits 1, and the fixes were verified by deliberately breaking things; the only small blemish is that assert_slug now merges stderr into the compared output with `2>&1`, which could cause a spurious mismatch if slugify.sh ever writes to stderr on success."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Only test/run-tests.sh changed, while the tests, their names, the FAIL/Results format, the non-zero exit, the script under test and its fixtures were all left alone (the broken files were restored), and the workflow was deliberately not touched; the stderr merge in assert_slug is a minor unrequested change in behavior."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply names the real failure mode: under `set -euo pipefail`, a command substitution that exits non-zero on a normal test result (grep no-match, cmp difference, slugify crash) kills the whole run. It describes the fix and the verification for each helper, though it could have said more explicitly that the abort hid the Results line and every later test."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.0
  },
